      "assistant_text": "According to [[credential-scoping]], the Anthropic API key is **injected into the spawned child process\u0027s environment immediately before that process starts**. \n\nSpecifically, the page says:\n\n- The Hub never holds the API key in its own process environment\n- A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n- The key is injected **only into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process**, right before that process starts\n- The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated\n\nThe same pattern applies to the Query agent \u2014 it also receives the credential injected into its own child process environment at spawn time, rather than inheriting it from the Hub.\n\nThe key point is that the injection happens into the **child process\u0027s environment**, keeping the credential isolated and preventing a compromised Hub process from accessing it through its own environment variables.",
      "input_tokens": 5199,
      "output_tokens": 192
    }
